diff --git a/tools/gogen/README.md b/tools/gogen/README.md
index 3b80057..cd1116d 100644
--- a/tools/gogen/README.md
+++ b/tools/gogen/README.md
@@ -1756,3 +1756,38 @@ private instance attributes. The static owned fixture checks constructor
 initialization, snapshots, section reads, stores, self-append and reset between
 test classes. Friend pools and reference actuals keep string storage. The
 generated 16-page equal-length store allocates zero bytes.
+
+## Base64 text decoding: cl_http_utility=>decode_base64 (2026-10-11)
+
+`decode_base64` was the last kernel line of `cl_http_utility` without a host
+function: any class calling it was `NOT_COMPILED`. Its ABAP on Node is
+`Buffer.from(encoded, "base64").toString( )`, and the reference is Node's
+answer, not A4H's (a system decodes the bytes in its code page; unmeasured).
+
+Two pieces, one per half of that line:
+
+- `go/nodeutf8` — `Decode(b string) string`, the WHATWG "UTF-8 decode"
+  algorithm without BOM that `Buffer.prototype.toString( )` runs: valid
+  multibyte UTF-8 becomes its characters, and every *maximal subpart* of an
+  ill-formed sequence becomes exactly one U+FFFD, so the valid text around
+  malformed bytes survives (`strings.ToValidUTF8` would collapse a whole
+  run into one). An invalid continuation ends the subpart and is read again
+  as the start of the next sequence; the narrowed first continuation after
+  `E0`, `ED`, `F0` and `F4` is what rejects overlong forms, surrogates and
+  code points above U+10FFFF; a lead byte left without its continuations at
+  the end is one U+FFFD; a byte order mark stays a character. Valid UTF-8
+  (the common case) returns unchanged. `go/apc` holds the same algorithm
+  inline for query strings.
+- `abap.DecodeBase64` (`go/abap/http_utility.go`) — `decode_x_base64`'s
+  base64 step (both alphabets, mixed included; padding optional; foreign
+  bytes ignored; decoding stops at the first `=`; a lone trailing character
+  is dropped) with the bytes read through `nodeutf8.Decode`. A NATIVE row
+  in the front end maps `CL_HTTP_UTILITY=>IF_HTTP_UTILITY~DECODE_BASE64` to
+  it, as `ENCODE_BASE64`'s row does for the other direction.
+
+The oracle: every 1-, 2- and 3-byte string over a lead/continuation
+alphabet and every 4-byte string over a lead-focused one — 12 522 inputs —
+decoded by `nodeutf8.Decode` and by Node 26.9, byte for byte the same.
+`go test ./nodeutf8/` and `TestDecodeBase64` pin the interesting rows;
+`ZCL_GOGEN_T_B64DEC` (semantics, `strlen( )` included: a supplementary
+character is two UTF-16 units) and its ABAP Unit rows run the compiled call.
