+// DecodeBase64 is cl_http_utility=>decode_base64: Buffer.from(encoded,
+// "base64").toString( ), the kernel lines of open-abap-core. The base64
+// step is decode_x_base64's (both alphabets, padding optional and foreign
+// bytes ignored), and the bytes are then read as text the way Node reads
+// them (go/nodeutf8): valid multibyte UTF-8 becomes its characters, and
